    <!-- Onboarding Guide -->
    <string name="onboarding_guide_title">Setup &amp; Remote Access Guide</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_pair">1. Get a pairing code</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_pair_desc">Run opencode pair in your terminal to display a QR code and pairing link.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_lan">2. Allow connections on your LAN</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_lan_desc">By default, OpenCode listens only on localhost. To allow access from your phone on the same Wi-Fi:\n• opencode service set hostname 0.0.0.0\n• opencode service start\n• opencode pair</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_ssh">3. SSH Port Forwarding</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_ssh_desc">If you don\'t want to bind to 0.0.0.0, forward port 4096 over SSH:\n• ssh -N -L 4096:localhost:4096 user@host\nThen connect to http://localhost:4096 on this device.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_tailscale">4. Tailscale &amp; VPN</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_tailscale_desc">With Tailscale installed on both your computer and phone, use your computer\'s Tailscale IP or MagicDNS hostname (e.g. http://my-mac:4096).</string>

